Fork modifications (PHP 7.4 → 8.5 port, dependency updates and removal,
documentation, security hardening — including an OpenID Connect
reimplementation replacing the EOL OpenID 2.0 stack): 2026, @deokio.

Nature of the modifications:

  The PHP 7.4 → 8.5 port consists predominantly of mechanical migrations
  following the official PHP upgrade documentation
  (https://www.php.net/migration80, .../migration81, .../migration82,
  .../migration83, .../migration84, .../migration85). Specifically:

    - PHP4-style constructor replacement (function ClassName → __construct)
    - Dynamic property declaration via #[AllowDynamicProperties] or
      explicit property declarations
    - mysqli procedural API → object-oriented API (1:1 mapping)
    - Implicit nullable parameter type fixes
    - ${} string interpolation replacement
    - Deprecated function replacement per official PHP migration guides

  Such mechanical transformations would yield substantially identical
  results regardless of who or what performs them, and are not considered
  to embody original creative authorship.

  A small number of components were newly authored as part of security
  hardening — notably a dependency-free OpenID Connect (OIDC) client
  (framework/legacy/Textcube.Control.OIDC.php) that replaces the
  end-of-life OpenID 2.0 implementation, and the removal of the bundled
  phpopenid library. These newly authored components are released under
  the GPL, consistent with the rest of the project.

  This work was performed with the assistance of an AI coding assistant
  (Anthropic Claude) under human review. The maintainer asserts no
  additional copyright over the mechanical migration changes themselves.

  No additional copyright is asserted over these modifications.
  All modifications are made available under the GNU General Public
  License (same as upstream).

